Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-16815-4_33","eisbn":["9783031168154"],"isbn":["9783031168147"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"600-605","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"International Conference on Applied Cryptography and Network Security"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140488787"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d75000b8-d44d-417d-aae5-41e671baf6e9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"POSTER: Enabling User-Accountable Mechanisms in Decision Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384438","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We study coercion-resistance for online exams. We propose two properties, Anonymous Submission and Single-Blindness which, if hold, preserve the anonymity of the links between tests, test takers, and examiners even when the parties coerce one another into revealing secrets. The properties are relevant: not even Remark!, a secure exam protocol that satisfied anonymous marking and anonymous examiners results to be coercion resistant. Then, we propose a coercion-resistance protocol which satisfies, in addition to known anonymity properties, the two novel properties we have introduced. We prove our claims formally in ProVerif. The paper has also another contribution: it describes an attack (and a fix) to an exponentiation mixnet that Remark! uses to ensure unlinkability. We use the secure version of the mixnet in our new protocol.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Giustolisi, Rosario"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382686"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coercion resistance","Exponentiation Mixnet","Formal verification","ProVerif","Security Flaws","Security Protocol Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"secure internet exams despite coercion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/ftp/arxiv/papers/2207/2207.12796.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382686","ids":["itu-5ea1a142-1f33-4672-b8ad-c87b7c5a7618"],"keyword":["Coercion-resistance","Exponentiation Mixnet","Formal Verification","Proverif","Security Flaws","Security Protocol Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-663DD6909F8BDE9B53C41293FBA3C341"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/ftp/arxiv/papers/2207/2207.12796.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"17th DPM International Workshop on Data Privacy Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5ea1a142-1f33-4672-b8ad-c87b7c5a7618"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Secure Internet Exams Despite Coercion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382686","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A choreography gives a description of how endpoints in a concurrent systems should exchange messages during its execution. In this paper, we informally introduce a choreographic language for describing security protocols and a property language for expressing non-trivial security properties of such protocols. We motivate this work using the envelope protocol [2] as an example, which ensures auditable transfers by means of a TPM, that guarantees that the issuer of a message always learns whether such message has been opened or not. We then take an implementation of the TPM formulated as an API and discuss how such implementation and the usage of the TPM in the protocol can be related. Finally, we illustrate how the protocol and property descriptions can be translated into multiset rewrite rules and metric first order logic respectively, in order to check if auditable transfer holds.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Carbone, Marco","Giustolisi, Rosario","Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-310372"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreography","Security protocols","Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"security protocols as choreographies","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-310372","identifier":[{"id":"85119665514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-13355403-b681-442d-9e5e-d2239d8a164e"],"keyword":["Choreography","Security protocols","Verification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EA9D1A4E0EF8BC005FCFD2FF0A70B10"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Formal Methods"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Marco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpau","last":"Mödersheim","locid":"21eb3855-68a7-4647-a3a0-8526af03169f","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","orcid":"0000-0002-6901-8319","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"doughertypedh","last":"Dougherty","name":"Dougherty, Daniel","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"meseguerpedh","last":"Meseguer","name":"Meseguer, José","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpedh","last":"Mödersheim","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"rowepedh","last":"Rowe","name":"Rowe, Paul","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-91631-2_5","isbn":["9783030916305"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"98-111","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Essays Dedicated to Joshua Guttman on the Occasion of his 66.66th Birthday","title":"Protocols, Strands, and Logic"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119665514"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-13355403-b681-442d-9e5e-d2239d8a164e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Security Protocols as Choreographies","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-310372","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"A choreography gives a description of how endpoints in a concurrent systems should exchange messages during its execution. In this paper, we informally introduce a choreographic language for describing security protocols and a property language for expressing non-trivial security properties of such protocols. We motivate this work using the envelope protocol [2] as an example, which ensures auditable transfers by means of a TPM, that guarantees that the issuer of a message always learns whether such message has been opened or not. We then take an implementation of the TPM formulated as an API and discuss how such implementation and the usage of the TPM in the protocol can be related. Finally, we illustrate how the protocol and property descriptions can be translated into multiset rewrite rules and metric first order logic respectively, in order to check if auditable transfer holds.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Carbone, Marco","Giustolisi, Rosario","Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381950"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Auditable Transfers","Choreographic Language","Multiset Rewrite Rules","Security protocols","Trusted Platform Module TPM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"security protocols as choreographies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381950","identifier":[{"id":"85119665514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2e5fa3e9-40e9-4a60-9ec5-30b1f20eb36c"],"keyword":["Auditable Transfers","Choreographic Language","Multiset Rewrite Rules","Security Protocols","Trusted Platform Module (TPM)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FF5FA21AA3B264DC55D51E3BCD2AF690"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpau","last":"Mödersheim","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"98","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Joshua Guttman's Festschrift","title":"Security Protocols as Choreographies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2e5fa3e9-40e9-4a60-9ec5-30b1f20eb36c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Security Protocols as Choreographies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381950","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Dispute resolution mechanisms are important components of voting schemes, deterring a voting authority to change the election outcome as any alteration can be proved by such mechanisms. However, these mechanisms are useless if not triggered by voters, who should not have to choose to either raise a dispute or keep their vote private. Hence, voting schemes should include privacy-preserving dispute resolution. In this work, we advance the formal analysis in the symbolic model of an improved version of the Bingo Voting scheme, whose enhancements include privacy-preserving dispute resolution mechanisms. Most of our analysis of several verification, dispute resolution, and privacy properties is done automatically using ProVerif, which we complement with manual induction proofs as necessary. We find that the scheme meets some properties only if one makes additional trust assumptions to those stated in [6]. For example, we find that dispute resolution is met assuming an honest voting authority. Moreover, our work provides an understanding of privacy-preserving dispute resolution in general, which can be beneficial to similar analyses of other voting schemes.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Giustolisi, Rosario","Bruni, Alessandro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383722"],"event":{"acronym":"E-VOTE-ID","title":"International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dispute Resolution","Election Security","Privacy Preserving Protocols","ProVerif Analysis","Voting schemes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"privacy preserving dispute resolution in the improved bingo voting","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85408382/Giustolisi_Bruni2020_Chapter_Privacy_PreservingDisputeResol.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383722","identifier":[{"id":"85092136879","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a8ae9bd6-1b87-4897-9a47-e15cd6cb0a3c"],"keyword":["Dispute Resolution","Election Security","Privacy-Preserving Protocols","ProVerif Analysis","Voting Schemes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A46791A8BAE772264C159BF947473527"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85408382/Giustolisi_Bruni2020_Chapter_Privacy_PreservingDisputeResol.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-60347-2_5","isbn":["9783030603465","9783030603472"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"67-83","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"E-Vote-ID: International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092136879"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a8ae9bd6-1b87-4897-9a47-e15cd6cb0a3c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Privacy-Preserving Dispute Resolution in the Improved Bingo Voting","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383722","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Static analysis is a tried-and-tested approach to eliminate vulnerabilities in software. However, despite decades of successful use by experts, mainstream programmers often deem static analysis too costly to use. Mainstream programmers do routinely use linters, which are static analysis tools geared towards identifying simple bugs and stylistic issues in software. Can linters serve as a medium for delivering vulnerability detection to mainstream programmers? We investigate the extent of which linters can be leveraged to help programmers write secure software. We present new rules for ESLint that detect---and automatically fix---certain classes of cross-site scripting, SQL injection, and misconfiguration vulnerabilities in JavaScript. Evaluating our experience, we find that there is enormous potential in using linters to eliminate vulnerabilities in software, due to the relative ease with which linter rules can be implemented and shared to the community. We identify several open challenges, including third-party library dependencies and linter configuration, and propose ways to address them.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rafnsson, Willard","Giustolisi, Rosario","Kragerup, Mark","Høyrup, Mathias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384822"],"event":{"acronym":"NSS","title":"International Conference on Network and System Security"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["JavaScript security","Linters","Mainstream programmers","Software vulnerabilities","Static analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fixing vulnerabilities automatically with linters","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85509700/2020nss_rafnsson_giustolisi_kragerup_hoeyrup.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384822","ids":["itu-f1832abc-21b8-4234-9b3c-e57f4d427ef9"],"keyword":["JavaScript security","Linters","Mainstream programmers","Software vulnerabilities","Static analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-36A98220639D53BB66578717112C7661"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85509700/2020nss_rafnsson_giustolisi_kragerup_hoeyrup.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Willard","key":"rafnssonpau","last":"Rafnsson","locid":"9cf737ee-bd9a-4f7e-b865-b6ff6ed01fde","name":"Rafnsson, Willard","orcid":"0000-0003-1482-3094","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"krageruppau","last":"Kragerup","name":"Kragerup, Mark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"høyruppau","last":"Høyrup","name":"Høyrup, Mathias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-65745-1","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"14th International Conference on Network and System Security"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f1832abc-21b8-4234-9b3c-e57f4d427ef9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fixing Vulnerabilities Automatically with Linters","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384822","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Giustolisi, Rosario"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384477"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"session details theme system software and security sec computer security track","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dje","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85408447/editorialsac20.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384477","ids":["itu-da220293-3f27-42cf-9a57-5a04bccd176b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-58F154996C06AC9FBBE629FC2BCCB821"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85408447/editorialsac20.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"ACM Symposium on Applied Computing,","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Symposium on Applied Computing,"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Cop