{"abstract":"We address the fundamental question of what are, and how to define, the threat models for a security protocol and its expected human users, the latter pair forming a heterogeneous system that is typically called a security ceremony. Our contribution is the systematic definition of an encompassing method to build the full threat model chart for security ceremonies, from which one can conveniently reify the specific threat models of interest for the ceremony under consideration. For concreteness, we demonstrate the application of the method on three ceremonies that have already been considered in the literature: MP-Auth, Opera Mini and the Danish Mobilpendlerkort ceremony. We discuss how the full threat model chart suggests some interesting threats that haven’t been investigated although they are well worth of scrutiny. In particular, one of the threat models in our chart leads to a novel vulnerability of the Danish Mobilpendlerkort ceremony. We discovered the vulnerability by analysing this threat model using the formal and automated tool Tamarin, which we employed to demonstrate the relevance of our method, but it is important to highlight that our method is generic and can be used with any tool for the analysis of security protocols and ceremonies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sempreboni, Diego","Bella, Giampaolo","Giustolisi, Rosario","Vigano, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384000"],"event":{"acronym":"ICETE","title":"International Joint Conference on E-business and Telecommunications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Formal analysis","Human factors","Security ceremonies","Threat models","Vulnerability discovery"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what are the threats charting the threat models of security ceremonies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5220/0007924901610172","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384000","identifier":[{"id":"85073054505","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bb111113-16d6-4418-aa56-e884c2730684"],"keyword":["Formal analysis","Human factors","Security ceremonies","Threat models","Vulnerability discovery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B5458AADEB8287A8C86EE0231093FB1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84735316/SECRYPT_2019_54_CR.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5220/0007924901610172","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diego","key":"semprebonipau","last":"Sempreboni","name":"Sempreboni, Diego","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Giampaolo","key":"bellapau","last":"Bella","name":"Bella, Giampaolo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"viganopau","last":"Vigano","name":"Vigano, Luca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5220/0007924901610172","eisbn":["9789897583780"],"publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 16th International Joint Conference on e-Business and Telecommunications","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073054505"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bb111113-16d6-4418-aa56-e884c2730684"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What Are the Threats? (Charting the Threat Models of Security Ceremonies)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384000","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The process that allows one to get rewarded for returning a container through reverse vending machines (RVM) involves people and technology. In fact, it typically sees a set of human parties (e.g. customers, cashiers) and technical parties (e.g, RVMs, databases, scanners) to collaborate in order to enable eective recycling. In this paper, we advance a formal treatment of the Danish Deposit Return System (DRS). We investigate the security of the ceremony that people are expected to perform in the context of DRS using eld observation and automated reasoning tools. We give a particular focus to the security threats due to people interacting with the technology behind DRS. The ndings of our investigation enable novel considerations of the ceremony weaknesses and make it possible to delineate potential mitigations.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Garbacz, Ivan","Giustolisi, Rosario","Møller Nielsen, Kasper","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382429"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automated Reasoning Tools","Deposit Return System DRS","Human Technology Interaction","Reverse Vending Machines RVM","Security Threats"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a security analysis of the danish deposit return system","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84679400/human.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382429","ids":["itu-4dbe548b-6320-4e73-a043-ed092ede44af"],"keyword":["Automated Reasoning Tools","Deposit Return System (DRS)","Human-Technology Interaction","Reverse Vending Machines (RVM)","Security Threats"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B97D8204CE224060F96037E63A50A7C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84679400/human.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan","key":"garbaczpau","last":"Garbacz","name":"Garbacz, Ivan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"møllernielsenpau","last":"Møller Nielsen","name":"Møller Nielsen, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th Workshop on Socio-Technical Aspects in Security and Trust"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4dbe548b-6320-4e73-a043-ed092ede44af"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Security Analysis of the Danish Deposit Return System","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382429","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
